The remaining proof branch is a standard symbolic “unknown tag” problem: the prover will not automatically decompose an arbitrary `Val` before evaluating `isinstance`. I’m making the list datatype explicitly tagged (`intCons`, `floatCons`, `boolCons`, `listCons`), so induction covers every modeled Python value category while each loop step still executes the translated `isinstance` and arithmetic statements.
